# Organisation-specific strings that must never reach a public commit.
# Copy to `.leakpatterns` (gitignored) and edit. One regex per line, matched
# case-insensitively; `#` starts a comment.
#
# Keep this list OUT of version control. A denylist committed to a public
# repository publishes exactly the identifiers it is meant to suppress.

# mycompany
# \bmycorp[-_]
# 1234567890            # internal GCP project number
# internal_dataset_name
# alice|bob             # personal handles that should not appear in the tree

# Exemptions: a line containing this literal string is skipped entirely.
# Use for a repository's own public URL, which necessarily contains the org name.
# !myorg/my-public-repo
